"""deck_icons.py — resolved snapshot of a curated subset of the design
system's 181-icon set (components/atomic/icon/svg/24x24/), extracted for use
as NATIVE pptx vector shapes rather than raster pictures — consistent with
deck_pptx.py's whole premise of real, editable shapes.

Each entry is the list of `d` path strings from that icon's <path
stroke="currentColor"> element(s) (a stray fill="white" artboard rect some
exports carry is filtered out — see the design system's memory note on this).
Only icons whose paths use exclusively M/L/H/V/C/Z commands (no arcs) are
included, since that's what deck_pptx.py's `_draw_icon` custGeom renderer
supports. All are 24x24 viewBox, stroke-width 2, round linecap — deck_pptx.py
renders them stroke-only (no fill), matching the source exactly.

To add another icon: pull its `d` string(s) the same way (skip any path
whose stroke isn't "currentColor"), confirm it uses only M/L/H/V/C/Z, and add
an entry here. If it uses an arc ("A"/"a"), it is not supported by the
current renderer — fall back to a numbered badge for that card instead.

Regenerate/extend via the extraction approach used to build this file:
walk components/atomic/icon/svg/24x24/, keep <path stroke="currentColor">
`d` strings, reject any using unsupported commands.
"""

